commit_template_hash: 686bd6f6d3f60a9716f8ca85195b61c4852e2e6d8a91cf7a01fc867d6252a9af
intent: Fix transcript_rate_limited's status check: an exact 'status != allowed' comparison treated 'allowed_warning' (a real, common status meaning still-allowed-but-utilization-climbing) as a throttling incident, crashing an N=10/v3 nool_try rerun before a single ticket finished. Discovered because same-day heavy real-agent usage across many benchmark runs pushed the account's 5-hour window to 93-94% utilization with overage unavailable, which is exactly when 'allowed_warning' starts appearing. Changed to a startswith('allowed') check so both 'allowed' and 'allowed_warning' pass; only a genuinely non-allowed status (denied/blocked/etc.) now triggers RateLimitAbort
knot_id: fae154a85c4bd1e20aaf60b8f8a80e9a70b81cc47410333b126318c60fce2284
